{"candidate_id":"figure-analysis:Figure4:73de580fc4761c72","artifact_id":"Figure4","visual_type":"flowchart","description":"Grouped bar chart of user-study ratings for automated movie generation. It compares VGoT, Mora, MovieAgent, and ReCA (Ours) across six human-rating criteria on a 0–5 scale; whiskers show per-cell standard error, and higher ratings are better.","components":[{"name":"VGoT","role":"comparison method","visual_evidence":"Light-blue bars appear in each of the six criterion groups."},{"name":"Mora","role":"comparison method","visual_evidence":"Light-green bars appear in each of the six criterion groups."},{"name":"MovieAgent","role":"comparison method","visual_evidence":"Pale-yellow bars appear in each of the six criterion groups."},{"name":"ReCA (Ours)","role":"evaluated method","visual_evidence":"Orange bars are tallest in all six groups, with labeled values 4.27, 3.99, 4.25, 3.62, 3.74, and 3.76."},{"name":"Visual Appeal","role":"rating criterion","visual_evidence":"First x-axis group; values are 1.12, 2.66, 2.04, and 4.27 for VGoT, Mora, MovieAgent, and ReCA."},{"name":"Script Faithfulness","role":"rating criterion","visual_evidence":"Second x-axis group; values are 1.07, 2.50, 1.98, and 3.99."},{"name":"Character Consistency","role":"rating criterion","visual_evidence":"Third x-axis group; values are 1.20, 1.81, 1.71, and 4.25."},{"name":"Background Consistency","role":"rating criterion","visual_evidence":"Fourth x-axis group; values are 1.22, 2.06, 1.82, and 3.62."},{"name":"Physical Law","role":"rating criterion","visual_evidence":"Fifth x-axis group; values are 1.13, 2.14, 2.13, and 3.74."},{"name":"Narrative Coherence","role":"rating criterion","visual_evidence":"Sixth x-axis group; values are 1.59, 2.45, 2.33, and 3.76."}],"relationships":[{"source_component":"VGoT","relation":"is compared on","target_component":"Visual Appeal"},{"source_component":"Mora","relation":"is compared on","target_component":"Script Faithfulness"},{"source_component":"MovieAgent","relation":"is compared on","target_component":"Character Consistency"},{"source_component":"ReCA (Ours)","relation":"has the highest rating for","target_component":"Visual Appeal"},{"source_component":"ReCA (Ours)","relation":"has the highest rating for","target_component":"Script Faithfulness"},{"source_component":"ReCA (Ours)","relation":"has the highest rating for","target_component":"Character Consistency"},{"source_component":"ReCA (Ours)","relation":"has the highest rating for","target_component":"Background Consistency"},{"source_component":"ReCA (Ours)","relation":"has the highest rating for","target_component":"Physical Law"},{"source_component":"ReCA (Ours)","relation":"has the highest rating for","target_component":"Narrative Coherence"}],"findings":["ReCA (Ours) is highest on all six rating criteria.","ReCA's highest displayed score is 4.27 for Visual Appeal, closely followed by 4.25 for Character Consistency.","ReCA's lowest displayed score is 3.62 for Background Consistency.","Mora is the strongest baseline on Visual Appeal, Script Faithfulness, Background Consistency, and Physical Law, while MovieAgent is slightly higher on Character Consistency and Narrative Coherence.","The y-axis spans human ratings from 0 to 5, and each bar has an error whisker."],"citations":[{"section_id":"sec-1~4","path_id":"1~4","quote":"Figure 4 User-study ratings for automated movie generation."},{"section_id":"sec-1~4","path_id":"1~4","quote":"Grouped bars compare VGoT, Mora, MovieAgent, and ReCA on six human-rating criteria"},{"section_id":"sec-1~4","path_id":"1~4","quote":"Whiskers report the per-cell standard error of the mean across raters; bars use a light colorblind-friendly palette; higher is better."},{"section_id":"sec-1~4","path_id":"1~4","quote":"ReCA wins every criterion (Figure 4: 4.27, 3.99, 4.25, 3.62, 3.74, 3.76 in that order)"}],"confidence":0.99,"provenance":{"image_sha256":"aee5d48fc73942ab27bf547bb54fe764def12c610ae30fa56ebf71a37491d4d3